tes bear the marks of countless battles and ancient curses."},{"id":"marker229","name":"Marshleach Necropolis","legend":"A foreboding necropolis perched atop a jagged cliff, overlooking a desolate wasteland. Its towering walls harbor restless spirits, and the imposing gates bear the marks of countless battles and ancient curses."},{"id":"marker230","name":"Dudley Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Suzetagan Campaign. \r\nDate: September 18, 1989 Kiney Era."},{"id":"marker231","name":"Disturbed Burial","legend":"A burial site has been disturbed in this area, causing the dead to rise and attack the living."},{"id":"marker232","name":"Piniontion Pillar","legend":"An ancient pillar. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">༱༤༗༆༆༚་་༑༁༬༗༂༶༉༂༱༦༧༖༱༇༵༅༐༘༅༄༬༫༮༛༗༖༫༣༡༰༴༌༘༑༦༫༃༤༃༧༖༜༗༯༚༔༧༗༰༺༕༂༖༛༧༑༳༅་༺༰༩༥༛༈༑༒ༀ༑༠༇༩༁༄༅༮༰༺༕༹༬༗༲༅༼༴</div>"},{"id":"marker233","name":"Disturbed Burial","legend":"A burial site has been disturbed in this area, causing the dead to rise and attack the living."},{"id":"marker235","name":"Ruined Outpost","legend":"Ruins of an ancient outpost. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker236","name":"Hubrossa Chasm","legend":"The Hubrossa Chasm. Locals claim that it is totally empty."},{"id":"marker238","name":"Teossos Megalith","legend":"An ancient megalith. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">ዘበ  ጰረአጰዘፐመጠኀከቀዐከዐየዐፐ መቀየየኀደፈረረሀጰወኀተወ ሀዐ ሠቀገሐገነ ቀጸሐሠቀአበሀጰተከገ ጠቀ ሰፐዘሠፀሀደሀከረወከደኀጸደሠመመሠሰአአደከኀመወኀገ</div>"},{"id":"regiment1-0","name":"1st (Jiliang) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 3 Kiney Era during the Tunumian War. 1st (Jiliang) Regiment is stationed in Jiliang Landgrave. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 121 KE:\r\n— infantry: 2022\r\n— archers: 1014\r\n— cavalry: 936\r\n— artillery: 9."},{"id":"regiment1-1","name":"2nd (Lingy) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1 Kiney Era during the Tunumian War. 2nd (Lingy) Regiment is stationed in Lingy Earldom. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 121 KE:\r\n— infantry: 1565\r\n— archers: 789\r\n— cavalry: 728\r\n— artillery: 7."},{"id":"regiment1-2","name":"3rd (Dih Guo) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 2 Kiney Era during the Gagatian War. 3rd (Dih Guo) Regiment is stationed in Dih Guo Captaincy. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 121 KE:\r\n— infantry: 1281\r\n— archers: 661\r\n— cavalry: 656\r\n— artillery: 6."},{"id":"regiment1-3","name":"4th (Shaozhou) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 121 Kiney Era during the Mandia-Gagatian War. 4th (Shaozhou) Regiment is stationed in Luangan. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 121 KE:\r\n— infantry: 1192\r\n— archers: 635\r\n— cavalry: 532\r\n— artillery: 7."},{"id":"regiment1-4","name":"5th (Danyang) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 2 Kiney Era during the Tunumian War. 5th (Danyang) Regiment is stationed in Danyang Captaincy. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 121 KE:\r\n— infantry: 965\r\n— archers: 505\r\n— cavalry: 445\r\n— artillery: 8."},{"id":"regiment1-5","name":"6th (Gaozhou) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 5 Kiney Era during the Bornian War. 6th (Gaozhou) Regiment is stationed in Gaozhou County. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 121 KE:\r\n— cavalry: 517\r\n— infantry: 914\r\n— archers: 462\r\n— artillery: 3."},{"id":"regiment1-6","name":"7th (Shouchun Guo) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 2 Kiney Era during the Gagatian War. 7th (Shouchun Guo) Regiment is stationed in Shouchun Guo County. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 121 KE:\r\n— infantry: 891\r\n— archers: 509\r\n— cavalry: 389\r\n— artillery: 4."},{"id":"regiment1-7","name":"8th (Nin Guo) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 119 Kiney Era during the Mandia-Gagatian War. 8th (Nin Guo) Regiment is stationed in Nin Guo County. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 121 KE:\r\n— infantry: 884\r\n— archers: 491\r\n— cavalry: 405\r\n— artillery: 2."},{"id":"regiment1-8","name":